# BYTE-IDENTITY DIRECTORY. These files are persisted scratch whose sha256 is
# the proof a future lane is running the same instrument, so git must do NO
# line-ending conversion in EITHER direction. The repo has core.autocrlf=true
# in the shared .git/config, which would rewrite the LF .py files to CRLF on
# checkout and normalise the CRLF reference outputs to LF on commit - both
# would break the sha256 table in README.md.
#
# Measured 2026-10-17: the .py and .md files are LF; reference/*.txt are CRLF
# because Python print() emits CRLF to a redirected file on Windows. Mixed on
# purpose - these are the bytes 0380 produced.
* -text
